  "text": "CG\nЦГ\nEN\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAccessibility\nHomepage\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs\nDiplomatic missions\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nJamaica\nJamaica*\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nJamaica\nVisa regime\nNationals of Jamaica are required to obtain a visa to enter Montenegro.\nVisas may be obtained from diplomatic and consular posts of Montenegro. If you are unable to reach a diplomatic or consular post of Montenegro, you may apply for a visa at the nearest diplomatic or consular post of the Republic of Serbia.\nContact: the Embassy of the Republic of Serbia in Havana, Republic of CubaAddress: 5ta Avenida, No. 4406, entre 44 y 46, Miramar Playa, La Habana, CubaPhone: + 53 / 7204-24-88+ 53 / 7204-26-07Email: officesrbhav@gmail.comambasadorsrbhav@gmail.comkonzsrbhav@gmail.comWebsite: http://www.havana.mfa.gov.rs\nDiplomatic relations\nJamaica officially recognized Montenegro on November 12, 2010, when diplomatic relations were established.\nHomepage\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAsk the Government\nPR contacts\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYouTube\nFlickr\nePayment\neHealth\neGovernment\nеTax\neEnrollment\nCentral Register of Business Entities\nAccessibility\nSite map\nEnglish\n©Copyright 2026. Government of MontenegroOpšti uslovi korišćenjaThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and applies Googleprivacy policyandterms of serice.",
